`@NotNull final ActionGroup group` confirmed — passing null `myPopupActions` here triggers an `IllegalArgumentException` via the `@NotNull` parameter assertion, exactly matching "IAE: PopupHandler.installPopupHandler". Since this eager, immediate-evaluation call was introduced by commit `6b3ab5d1791`, replacing the old lazy anonymous-listener version (which only read `myPopupActions` later, at actual popup time — by then already assigned), that's the bug-introducing commit.

## Bug-Introducing Commits
BIC: 6b3ab5d1791ad07bc3af4fe8bb3e57b6ed2a9662

## Reasoning

**(1) Investigation:** The fix commit reorders two statements in `FileHistoryPanelImpl`'s constructor so `myPopupActions = createPopupActions();` happens *before* `createDualView()`. I used `git log -L` on the two `PopupHandler.installPopupHandler(...)` lines inside `createDualView()` to trace their history, and checked the constructor's statement order at each prior revision.

**(2) The introducing change:** In commit `6b3ab5d1791` ("vcs: use util method", Feb 11 2016), the two mouse-listener registrations were refactored from:
```java
myDualView.getTreeView().addMouseListener(new PopupHandler() {
  public void invokePopup(...) {
    ... myPopupActions ... // read lazily, only when user actually right-clicks
  }
});
```
to:
```java
PopupHandler.installPopupHandler(myDualView.getTreeView(), myPopupActions, ActionPlaces.UPDATE_POPUP, ActionManager.getInstance());
```
This changed `myPopupActions` from a value read *lazily* inside an anonymous listener (only invoked later, after the constructor fully finished and the field was assigned) to a value read *eagerly* as a method argument, evaluated immediately when `createDualView()` runs. `PopupHandler.installPopupHandler`'s `group` parameter is annotated `@NotNull`, so passing the still-`null` `myPopupActions` throws an `IllegalArgumentException` — matching the "IAE: PopupHandler.installPopupHandler" bug report.

